    "text": "[Patient ID: P-10023 | Name: Robert Chen | Type: soap_note | Date: 2025-08-10T14:30:00Z]\nSOAP NOTE - Encounter Date: 2025-08-10. Subjective: 47-year-old male presents for 6-month hypertension follow-up. Reports mild occasional headaches and mild exertion dyspnea. Adherence to Lisinopril is consistent. Objective: BP 138/88 mmHg, HR 72 bpm, SpO2 98% on room air. BMI 28.4. Lungs clear to auscultation bilaterally. Heart: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs. Assessment: Essential hypertension, suboptimally controlled; Stage 1. Plan: Increase Lisinopril from 10mg daily to 20mg daily orally. Order basic metabolic panel (BMP) to check electrolytes and creatinine in 4 weeks. Return for BP check in 6 weeks.",
