    "text": "[Patient ID: P-10024 | Name: Jane Doe | Type: soap_note | Date: 2025-07-15T11:00:00Z]\nSOAP NOTE - Encounter Date: 2025-07-15. Subjective: 39-year-old female presents with seasonal allergic rhinitis, sneezing, nasal congestion, and itchy watery eyes for 3 weeks. No fever or purulent drainage. Known severe allergy to Penicillin (causes hives/anaphylaxis). Objective: Vital signs stable, afebrile. HEENT: Pale, boggy nasal turbinates with clear rhinorrhea. Conjunctival injection bilaterally. Assessment: Moderate allergic rhinitis. Plan: Start Fluticasone propionate nasal spray 50mcg, 2 sprays per nostril once daily. Cetirizine 10mg daily as needed. Strict avoidance of Penicillin and beta-lactam class antibiotics noted in chart.",
